    "text_delta": "I look ahead to future senior opportunities, understanding the panel's perspective on where I scored well and areas where I can develop would be very valuable.\"*\n2. **Review the feedback objectively:**  \n   Once received, examine the competency scores and specific remarks. Look for clues about what the panel felt was missing or where the successful candidate scored higher.\n3. **Only escalate if there is clear procedural irregularity:**  \n   In the civil service, appeals or grievances generally require demonstrable procedural errors (e.g., failure to adhere to the published merit principles, conflicts of interest, or documented bias). Unless the formal feedback or process records reveal a clear breach of civil service recruitment code, raising panel demographics will almost certainly be counterproductive.\n",
